From: Paul Philippov <paul@themactep.com>
Subject: [PATCH] t20: keep a usable scaler cap when crop is disabled

isp_core_frame_channel_scaler_capture() derived the scaler input size
from attr->output.fmt.pix.{width,height}, which is only latched by
isp_core_frame_channel_set_crop() when crop is enabled.  With crop
disabled those stay 0, so scalercap.max_width/max_height collapsed to 0
and frame_channel_set_scaler_info() then rejected every SET_SCALER with
EINVAL:

    [KernelIF] T20 SET_SCALER failed: Invalid argument
    [ERROR:IMPFramesource.cpp]: IMP_FrameSource_EnableChn(1) ... failed

When crop is off the scaler input is the full frame, so fall back to the
sensor mbus size instead of the unlatched 0.

Signed-off-by: Paul Philippov <paul@themactep.com>
---
 driver/t20/sdk/source/apical-isp/tx-isp-core.c | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/driver/t20/sdk/source/apical-isp/tx-isp-core.c b/driver/t20/sdk/source/apical-isp/tx-isp-core.c
--- a/driver/t20/sdk/source/apical-isp/tx-isp-core.c
+++ b/driver/t20/sdk/source/apical-isp/tx-isp-core.c
@@ -1462,6 +1462,13 @@
 	} else {
 		inwidth = attr->output.fmt.pix.width;
 		inheight = attr->output.fmt.pix.height;
+		if (inwidth == 0 || inheight == 0) {
+			/* Crop disabled: output size was never latched, so the
+			 * scaler input is the full frame.  Without this the cap
+			 * collapses to 0 and every SET_SCALER is rejected. */
+			inwidth = mbus->width;
+			inheight = mbus->height;
+		}
 		attr->scalercap.min_width = attr->min_width;
 		attr->scalercap.min_height = attr->min_height;
 	}
